<title>JAPAN: Thai's Bangchak tenders to buy July crude.</title>
<headline>Thai's Bangchak tenders to buy July crude.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Bangchak Petroleum Plc has issued a tender to buy 500,000 barrels of Middle East crude oil and 600,000 barrels of Far East crude oil for July loading, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on Wednesday, and offers should be valid for one day, traders said.</p>
<p>The Thai refiner often buys Oman crude, which was notionally assessed at a discount of about five to 10 cents to its official selling price in the recent physical market.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-5473-3706</p>
</text>
